          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"workers-use-case\">Workers use case</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">In this notebook, we will show a simple use case involving workers.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Prerequisites:</strong><br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- API token (see <a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/api/s3/tokens/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for info on how\n to create one);<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- at least one active worker.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "BYtC",
      "code_hash": "8e759ded24b1421fde1170a53ee0442f",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"ranking-workers-by-multiple-metrics\">Ranking workers by multiple metrics</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Here, we will show the top workers by 4 metrics also available in dash: requests, errors,\ndisconnects and median CPU time.\nResults are returned on a hourly basis, so here is how these metrics are aggregated:<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- requests are summed;<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- dash combines both errors and disconnects, here we show them standalone, summed as well;<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- cpu time is averaged out of all hourly 50th percentiles.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "emfo",
      "code_hash": "76b8f9693723b8985da0d2c9773a7ae0",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Raw data (includes all entries from GraphQL results):</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "dfe174b2e6b86cf8b6af00671b8cdea8",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Now, what we are interested in is comparing side by side these top entries for each metric.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><span style=\"color: tomato\"><b>Warning:</b> both the start and end of the obtained timeseries may have\nsharp drops due to aggregations on incomplete periods of time.<span></span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
